{
    "background_story": "Holland, a skilled archaeologist, had always been fascinated by the ancient Thracian civilization. Growing up in a family of historians, she spent countless hours poring over dusty tomes and crumbling scrolls. Her passion led her to Bulgaria, where she joined an excavation team uncovering the secrets of the Thracian kingdom. As she carefully brushed away the dirt from a recently unearthed artifact, Holland felt an inexplicable connection to the people who once called this land home. She spent years studying the Thracian culture, mastering their language, and learning their customs. Her expertise earned her the nickname 'The Thracian Whisperer' among her peers. Holland's love for the Thracians went beyond mere academic interest; she felt a deep sense of kinship with the fierce warriors and skilled artisans who once thrived in this ancient land.",
